  "dom_id": "questionExplanation-131400",
  "name": null,
  "problem": "",
  "worked_solution": "We're given that $Z∼N(0,1),$ and we wish to compute $P(Z\\ge -1.32).$ The required probability is represented by the area shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14254773/assets/d89bd5f38fdf4c952146dde8cd01207167c92cab07290742d229ceb0f4cf5712.png)\n\nBy the definition of the cumulative distribution function $Φ(z),$ \n\n$$\nP(Z\\le z)=Φ(z).\n$$\n\nSince the total area under the graph equals $1,$ we can express the required probability in terms of $Φ(z)$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(Z\\ge -1.32) & =1-P(Z<-1.32) \\\\  & =1-Φ(-1.32)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14254773/assets/0959a3c48bf70d10f24d85cd98bcd0703db4765ba5349d02896e18104c3f98a7.png)\n\nFrom the table, we know that\n\n$$\nΦ(-1.32)=0.0934.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(Z\\ge -1.32) & =1-Φ(-1.32) \\\\  & =1-0.0934 \\\\  & =0.9066.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
  "fields": [],
  "problem_field_keys": [],
  "answer_fields_complete": null,
  "result": null,
  "proof_feedback": null,
